    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Dear colleague,</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">We are delighted to confirm the speakers for our next webinar, <strong>Speed in Election Results Transmission</strong>, taking place on <strong>Tuesday, 14 July 2026 at 13:00&ndash;15:00 UTC (14:00&ndash;16:00 BST)</strong>.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Transparency and speed are two critical elements of election administration, especially in an always-on information environment. Both depend on the effective management of a myriad of interconnected processes, from results transmission at polling stations through to verification, aggregation, reconciliation, legal checks, and public communication.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 24px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">This webinar examines best practices across the full results workflow. It recognises that in many countries electoral laws and long-standing traditions mandate complex or slow procedures, and focuses on practical ways Election Management Bodies (EMBs) can improve efficiency, resilience, and transparency within those constraints.</p>

